**Criterion (`2 node dlm=tcp test 100% successful`) NOT met** — marker not written (honest). The full 2/tcp suite is 16/17 PASS; only `dir_reuse_coherency` fails (flaky). Build handed off: `6E20D7F9` (clean compile, deployed via the test runs).

### Major win — phantom-EX root found and fixed
The decisive infra bug: **`mxfs_v5_dlm_inode_held()` returned `1` (held) unconditionally on the TCP transport** (it only ever consulted the CAW slot table). That made the entire sess107 phantom-EX detection/fix infrastructure **inert on TCP** — the exact transport this criterion tests — for ~90 sessions. With a real TCP held-check (`mxfs_dlm_held_mode`, local-mirror lookup), I proved the phantom-EX: `P106-STALE-EX` fired 45× on node1 (`cached_mode=EX on_disk_held=0 unpub=1`) — node1 RMW'd the shared dir under a locally-granted **unpublished** EX invisible to the DLM, while node2 acquired the empty slot cleanly → concurrent divergent RMW → durable lost-update. Three landed fixes (broadened unpublished-EX backstop + un-throttled TCP held-verify/re-acquire) drove **`P106-STALE-EX` → 0**, eliminating the mutual-exclusion violation. These are real bug fixes worth keeping.

### Residual precisely characterized (RULE 4, with forensics)
Added content forensics (`P-DWR`/`P-DRD`, now gated behind `mxfs.dirwr`) that **proved** the remaining flaky failure is a **divergent block-0 cache via a lingering prior-incarnation buffer**: block 0 (at a reused daddr) oscillates `83↔100` on disk via xfsaild; failing runs read the stale `83` durably from disk. The release drain/stale completes cleanly (`P35F=0`, `P-SF-DURABLE-FAIL=0`), so it's not a release miss — it's node2's round-N (incarnation-N) buffer lingering at the reused daddr, served stale (read-hook `incarn_aba` check TRYLOCK-fails because node2's own xfsaild is destaging that dead buffer) and re-destaged → clobber.

### Next session
Three fix candidates recorded in memory (`sess-tcp-HANDOFF-phantom-ex-fixed-residual-incarn-aba`), top one: **discard `incarn_aba` dirty buffers** (xfs_da_btree.c ~3216) — a prior-incarnation buffer's dirty content is dead and must not be destaged. Also: `inode_mht_ms=300` must become the code default (needed for timing) before the criterion run.

